# Render tier benchmark: one run of the renderer on the current machine.
#
# Normally launched three times by scripts/bench_tiers.py (tier 0, tier 1 and
# the driver's choice), which collects the files and builds the comparison.
# By hand:
#
#   build/MineGame.exe --script scripts/bench_tier.mgs --script-out automation_out/bench_manual
#   build/MineGame.exe --script scripts/bench_tier.mgs --gl-tier 0 --script-out ...
#
# Writes surface.png/.json and underground.png/.json to the output directory,
# and three per-frame profiler captures next to the executable, in this order:
#   1. the load after the first teleport (mesh building and upload),
#   2. 10 seconds standing on the settled surface,
#   3. 10 seconds standing in the settled underground, where the most chunks
#      are submitted.
# The 10-second captures are wall-clock, so a slow machine records fewer frames
# of the same scene rather than the same frames more slowly.

/noclip 1

/profile start
/tp 500 90 500
look 0 -20
wait loaded
/profile stop

screenshot surface
state surface
/profile start 10
wait profile

/tp 0 -60 0
look 45 -10
wait loaded

screenshot underground
state underground
/profile start 10
wait profile

quit
